{"name":"Limeade","hex":"#5f9727","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"limeade","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A (variety of) citrus drink made from water, sugar, and the juice of limes.","A serving of this drink."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/limeade"}],"entries":[{"title":"Limeade","blocks":[{"text":"Limeade is a lime-flavored drink; when carbonated, it is also called lime soda. It is usually sweetened with sugar or sweeteners. A common method of preparation is to juice limes and combine the juice with simple syrup or honey syrup, along with some water and perhaps more sugar or honey. Vodka or white tequila can be added to make a limeade cocktail. The exact ingredients, preparation and names of the drink can vary by country."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Limeade.jpg/330px-Limeade.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Limeade","wikidata":"Q488482"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Koh_Mak%2C_Thailand%2C_Lime_juice_with_ice%2C_Lemonade%2C_Limeade.jpg/500px-Koh_Mak%2C_Thailand%2C_Lime_juice_with_ice%2C_Lemonade%2C_Limeade.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Koh_Mak%2C_Thailand%2C_Lime_juice_with_ice%2C_Lemonade%2C_Limeade.jpg/1280px-Koh_Mak%2C_Thailand%2C_Lime_juice_with_ice%2C_Lemonade%2C_Limeade.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Koh_Mak%2C_Thailand%2C_Lime_juice_with_ice%2C_Lemonade%2C_Limeade.jpg/500px-Koh_Mak%2C_Thailand%2C_Lime_juice_with_ice%2C_Lemonade%2C_Limeade.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Limeade with ice, Thailand","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKoh_Mak%2C_Thailand%2C_Lime_juice_